      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to replace a roof in Utah is during late spring, summer, or early fall when weather conditions are stable and temperatures consistently stay above 40\u00b0F to 50\u00b0F.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "late spring, summer, or early fall"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Ideal Seasons"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Late Spring to Early Fall: Warm and dry weather helps asphalt shingles seal correctly and adhesives activate under the sun."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Summer: Offers long daylight hours for contractors to finish the job quickly, though you should book early before peak demand."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why Avoid Winter in Utah?"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Cold Temperatures: Asphalt shingles can become brittle and crack in freezing mountain temperatures."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sealing Issues: Shingles need direct warmth from the sun to activate self-sealing strips. Cold weather can delay or prevent proper sealing, risking blow-offs during heavy winds."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Accumulation on the roof creates safety hazards and delays construction."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Signs It Is Time to Replace"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Age: Asphalt shingle roofs in Utah typically last 20 to 30 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Damage: Key signs that a roof may require replacement include its age (typically over 10-15 years, particularly for 3-tab shingles), visible missing shingles, or any evidence of water intrusion, leaks, or mold in the attic or interior of the home. -- .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://www.quora.com/My-contractor-says-I-need-a-10k-roof-makeover-but-when-I-came-outside-to-look-at-it-it-seems-perfectly-normal-except-for-a-couple-of-shingles-is-he-trying-to-rip-me-off-and-if-not-should-I-do-it"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Climate Wear: Utah's intense freeze-thaw cycles and heavy snow loads can speed up wear and tear on older materials."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
